A||||2||casto9||problems with an 87 gt||||1||
Z||000000||casto9||07-11-2000||09:37 AM||||I am 18 years old and have owned an 87 fiero gt for the past year and a half. I love the car but, it has high miles on it, and has quite a few problems. First of all, I was wondering if someone could tell me what is wrong when the tach needle doesn't stay still, it bounces around. Also, it feels kind of like the car isn't getting enough power from the engine when I accel. Second, I was wondering about the exhaust manifolds. Would these be the reason the car crackles after I release the accel.? I know I have problems with the exhaust system in general b/c the car is loud. (Not a good loud.) I have a limited budget and not too many mechanics around here know anything about fieros. I just spent over a thousand dollars to have a new clutch kit put in. That is why I would like to know a little about what is wrong so I don't just have to listen to a mechanic who has never touched a fiero tell me stuff. Thanks to anyone who answers.||||reg||1
Z||000001||lennyb4||07-11-2000||10:17 AM||||Well first off welcome to the best fiero forum around... I'll take a crack at this: If your tach is jumping around the first thing i would check would be the tach filter. When was the last time you gave your car a real good tune up (plugs,wires,filters, coils checked)? If your exaust is bad you can order a Gorlic system from the fiero store (around $120 w/o converter) and just get a tru-flow converter from summit racing for $45.00. Trust me when i say thats alot cheaper then you'll find it anywhere else. Its not the best or top of the line but it works and doesnt sound that bad either. <BR><p>[This message has been edited by lennyb4 (edited 07-11-2000).]||||reg||6
Z||000002||coyote||07-11-2000||10:18 AM||||welcome to the forum.<BR>the first thing i would check on is the tach filter, it is a small silver can located on by the coil. Does the engine seem to cycle with the tach movement, is it only at idle, does the car jerk at constant speed. when you say not enough power on accel, will the car turn the wheels over.as far as the exhaust manifolds, it is possible that one or both is cracked. the one at the front of the car is the one i would suspect first, water tends to drip on that manifold and after awhile it cracks, I do believe there was a recall that eliminated that problem 9 the other guys on the forum will be able to help you with that).<P>Coyote<BR>84 SE<BR>87 GT||||reg||1
